{"title":"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the radius of a circle is increased <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71bd818354ff89f378b1c6b3d4df72f3c8c508b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />, the area is increased:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/8/4687ebe6868abd52cdb3bf76d120c2a0b5a088ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 100\\%\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 200\\%\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 300\\%\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 400\\%\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{By none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"594\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Increasing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71bd818354ff89f378b1c6b3d4df72f3c8c508b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> is the same as doubling the radius. If we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the radius of the old circle, then the radius of the new circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/f/2cf2550f84107fd283d56c261aac3f13d226b0a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2r.$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Since the area of the circle is given by the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/8/ad87e482eae3848fa32bb915bbb3370f30df8bb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi r^2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"20\" /> the area of the new circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bc482c18b933eb8596a1a485af1b9ecc30f6346.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi (2r)^2 = 4\\pi r^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"19\" /> The area is quadrupled, or increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/b/4cb6509edf1edd4944946e643d648c99a52712ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(C) }300\\%.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"86\" height=\"29\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME\" title=\"1950 AHSME\">1950 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1950 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1950\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">